679
00:32:40.680 --> 00:32:47.060
This whole scene made me think of a college advertising class I had where we talked about subliminal messaging.

680
00:32:47.440 --> 00:32:51.580
Lady, we had that class in my high school, and I wrote my senior paper on the subject.

681
00:32:51.780 --> 00:32:52.680
Oh, my gosh.

682
00:32:53.420 --> 00:33:00.480
Well, I have nothing new to share with you then, Jenna, but I will tell you, here are a few things I found online, and I'm sure you can add to it.

683
00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:08.280
According to a website called HubSpot, subliminal messaging and advertising is designed to engage people subconsciously.

684
00:33:08.280 --> 00:33:17.900
These ads use various colors, shapes, and words that enable customers to make a small but powerful association between a brand and an intended meaning.

685
00:33:18.180 --> 00:33:22.020
As I looked up subliminal messaging, Jenna, one guy's name kept coming up.

686
00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:22.540
Who?

687
00:33:22.880 --> 00:33:24.720
James McDonald Vickery.

688
00:33:25.100 --> 00:33:26.040
What did he do?

689
00:33:26.240 --> 00:33:27.400
Get ready for this.

690
00:33:27.620 --> 00:33:32.060
The whole concept of subliminal messaging was first introduced by him.

691
00:33:32.060 --> 00:33:34.440
He was a marketing researcher, and in 1957,

692
00:33:34.440 --> 00:33:46.320
he claimed that he did an experiment in which moviegoers were repeatedly shown a 1,000-3,000-second advertisement saying something to the effect of,

693
00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:48.580
hungry, eat popcorn, drink Coca-Cola.

694
00:33:49.000 --> 00:33:58.300
Based on these claims, the CIA got involved and did a report called the Operational Potential of Subliminal Perception in 1958

695
00:33:58.300 --> 00:34:02.320
that led to subliminal cuts being banned in the U.S.

696
00:34:02.680 --> 00:34:03.180
Wow.

697
00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:05.620
The CIA suggested that, quote,

698
00:34:05.940 --> 00:34:13.680
certain individuals can at certain times and under certain circumstances be influenced to act abnormally without awareness of the influence.

699
00:34:13.960 --> 00:34:14.400
Wow.

700
00:34:14.720 --> 00:34:16.520
So here's the twiSt.

701
00:34:17.160 --> 00:34:22.800
Vickery provided no explanations for his results or any other details about his study to the public,

702
00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:25.520
claiming it was part of a confidential patent.

703
00:34:25.520 --> 00:34:32.080
Years later, Stuart Rogers interviewed the theater where Vickery supposedly conducted the experiment,

704
00:34:32.620 --> 00:34:36.720
and the theater manager said that no such test ever happened at that theater.

705
00:34:37.180 --> 00:34:37.800
What?

706
00:34:38.120 --> 00:34:46.740
In a television interview in 1962 for Advertising Age, Vickery admitted that the original study was a gimmick

707
00:34:46.740 --> 00:34:51.200
and that the amount of data was too small to be meaningful.

708
00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:55.120
After this interview, Vickery shied away from media attention,

709
00:34:55.360 --> 00:34:58.100
but his papers are held by the Thomas J.

710
00:34:58.300 --> 00:35:00.660
Dodd Research Center at the University of Connecticut.

711
00:35:01.020 --> 00:35:05.640
There have been many commentaries and theories about this since it happened.

712
00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.120
But I thought that was fascinating.

713
00:35:08.420 --> 00:35:13.220
That seems to disprove subliminal advertising works.

714
00:35:13.580 --> 00:35:15.100
Like it was a hoax.

715
00:35:15.100 --> 00:35:17.080
Yes, exactly.

716
00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:21.820
Supposedly, Vickery admitted that he never conducted the subliminal experiment,

717
00:35:22.440 --> 00:35:26.600
and it was a gimmick to attract customers to his failing marketing business.

718
00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.600
Oh my gosh.

719
00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:34.460
I know, but it started a whole conversation about marketing and advertising

720
00:35:34.460 --> 00:35:37.880
and how to attract people to your brand and make associations.

721
00:35:38.520 --> 00:35:44.440
This led me to a bunch of websites that talked about subliminal messagings and company logos,

